INT. CAROUSEL WORKSHOP - DAY

Painted horses hang from ceiling chains. Gold leaf. Sawdust. A radio plays accordion music.

XIMENA DELACROIX-ORTEGA (30s, tool belt, brush behind her ear) paints an eye on a wooden stallion.

A WOMAN enters. Grey raincoat. Umbrella dripping. She scans the room. Counts exits.

WOMAN
You're the restorer?

XIMENA
Depends who's asking.

WOMAN
Someone who needs the third horse from the left.

Ximena sets down the brush. Wipes her hands slowly.

XIMENA
That horse is spoken for.

WOMAN
By who?

PAVEL KORCHAK (60s, apron, glasses on a cord) emerges from behind a lion. Holds a mallet like a baton.

PAVEL
By me.

The woman smiles. Closes the umbrella.

WOMAN
Isolde Marchetti. Now we can all stop pretending.

XIMENA
Isolde. Right.

Beat. Pavel lowers the mallet.

PAVEL
You're early.

ISOLDE
Rain made the traffic light.

She approaches the third horse. Taps its hollow belly. A soft metallic ring.

ISOLDE (CONT'D)
Still sealed?

XIMENA
Gold leaf over solder.

ISOLDE
Good. Nobody looks at a gilded horse.

The accordion swells. Pavel turns the radio up.
